  "content": {
    "id": "p51-task75-78-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the maximum value of each of the following quadratic functions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p51-task75-78-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=-x^2+6x+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Maximum $11$ at $x=3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=-(x^2-6x)+2\\\\y&=-\\left[(x-3)^2-9\\right]+2\\\\y&=11-(x-3)^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe vertex is $(3,11)$ and the parabola is concave down. The maximum value is $11$, attained at $x=3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-task75-78-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=-3x^2+6x+7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Maximum $10$ at $x=1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=-3(x^2-2x)+7\\\\y&=-3\\left[(x-1)^2-1\\right]+7\\\\y&=10-3(x-1)^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe vertex is $(1,10)$ and the parabola is concave down. The maximum value is $10$, attained at $x=1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-task75-78-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=-2x^2-9x-4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p51-task75-78-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Maximum ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\dfrac{49}{8}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " at ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x=-\\dfrac94",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p51-task75-78-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Complete the square: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=\\dfrac{49}{8}-2\\left(x+\\dfrac94\\right)^2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=-2\\left(x^2+\\frac92x\\right)-4\\\\y&=-2\\left[\\left(x+\\frac94\\right)^2-\\frac{81}{16}\\right]-4\\\\y&=\\frac{49}{8}-2\\left(x+\\frac94\\right)^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe vertex is $\\left(-\\dfrac94,\\dfrac{49}{8}\\right)$ and the parabola is concave down. The maximum value is $\\dfrac{49}{8}$, attained at $x=-\\dfrac94$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
